00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.230
Maybe it was Rain.
也许是雷恩。

297
00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:06.450
And we stopped at one point and they, one or both of them got off and were like, I'm not getting back on this bus until you sort this out.
我们中途停了一次，他们其中一人或两人下了车，说：“在你们解决这个问题之前，我不会再上这辆巴士了。”

298
00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:10.970
But there was a real moment of like, hey, it's not just actors complaining in here.
但当时确实有一种感觉，就是：嘿，这里不只是演员在抱怨。

299
00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.470
There's, you should, this should be addressed.
这里有，你们应该，这事儿必须得解决。

300
00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:19.130
And then the other was, there was silence on that bus for a little while.
然后在那之后，巴士上安静了一会儿。

301
00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:28.210
And Ed, from the back, was like, 17 cast members of the office died today.
然后埃德从后面冒出一句，今天《办公室》剧组有17个成员去世了。

302
00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.010
Like, just peppered it out there and everybody started laughing.
就像是随口一说，然后大家都笑了起来。

303
00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:32.710
Did his Tom Brokaw.
他模仿了汤姆·布罗考。

304
00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:38.590
That he did his Brokaw, announcing that like the entire cast had been killed in a traffic accident.
他模仿布罗考播报说，整个剧组都在一场车祸中丧生了。

305
00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.250
And I was like, that's hilarious.
当时我就觉得，这太搞笑了。

306
00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:41.950
Like, that is so funny.
真的，太好笑了。

307
00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.850
In this moment where everyone's like, I can't, I can't, I will not stand for that.
在那个大家都在说“我受不了，我不能接受，我绝不容忍”的时刻。

308
00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:52.030
You know, silently stewing that he was like, from the deep, deep back of the bus.
你知道，他当时坐在大巴车最靠后的位置，心里默默地憋着坏。

309
00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.430
That's awesome.
那太棒了。

310
00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.610
Well, we remember Work Bus the same.
看来我们对《工作大巴》那集的记忆是一样的。

311
00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.130
That's really similar to our memories.
我们的记忆真的很相似。

312
00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:00.970
This is a crazy question.
这个问题有点疯狂。

313
00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.350
I feel like I know the answer.
我觉得我知道答案。

314
00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:07.490
Did you really grow a mustache for Movember, for the episode Movember?
你是真的为了“胡子月”活动，为了那一集《胡子月》留了胡子吗？

315
00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:09.370
Or was that a fakey mustache?
还是说那是假胡子？

316
00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.490
I have such a weak, such a weak mustache.
我的胡子长得特别稀疏，特别弱。

317
00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:18.770
I'll grow like an Amish kind of, you know, chin strap overnight.
我一夜之间只能长出那种阿米什人风格的下巴胡须。

318
00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:23.490
But the one thing I pine for is like a proper, I would just live with a cool,
但我一直渴望拥有一副像样的胡子，如果可以的话，我真想留着那种酷酷的……

319
00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.270
Selic mustache if I could.
汤姆·塞立克那样的胡子。

320
00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.490
So no, I didn't, I didn't do it.
所以没有，我没留胡子。

321
00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:33.530
They cut my hair, you know, just to maintain that men's bob that I had.
他们剪了我的头发，你知道，只是为了维持我当时那种男士波波头。

322
00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:41.410
And then used the ends of those clippings to make my own little rat stash that they taped on.
然后用那些剪下来的碎发做成了一个小胡茬，粘在我的嘴唇上。

323
00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.730
They used your own hair clippings to make that mustache?
他们用你自己的碎发做成了那个胡子？

324
00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:47.070
Yeah, yeah.
对，没错。

325
00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:51.250
I mean, it's kind of, it's both like overkill and also real attention to detail.
我是说，这既有点小题大做，又体现了对细节的极致追求。

326
00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:51.910
It's pretty cool.
这真的很酷。

327
00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:57.950
Also better than being like, I don't know, this is someone's hair and we'll just put it on.
而且总比用别人的头发粘在脸上要好，我不知道那是谁的头发。

328
00:16:58.270 --> 00:16:59.310
Oh, God.
天哪。

329
00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:06.890
I think you got the better deal than what Paul Lieberstein got because that was like a small woodland creature on his upper lip.
我觉得你比保罗·利伯斯坦幸运多了，因为他嘴唇上粘的那个看起来就像个小型林地生物。

330
00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:11.530
That's got to be fake too, right?
那肯定也是假的，对吧？

331
00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.330
That's not, he didn't grow.
那不是他自己长出来的吧。

332
00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:13.610
Oh, that was for sure fake.
哦，那绝对是假的。

333
00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.390
Okay.
好吧。

334
00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:19.450
I have to ask you about all of those diehard scenes.
我必须问问你关于那些《虎胆龙威》的戏份。

335
00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:23.990
I mean, I watched all the deleted scenes and there were so many, Jake.
我是说，我看了所有删减片段，真的有好多，杰克。

336
00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.230
It was physical too.
而且还有肢体动作。

337
00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:29.670
Like you were like rolling on the ground and standing up and it was amazing.
你又是滚地又是站起来，简直太精彩了。

338
00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:34.730
Yeah, I had, you know, my girlfriend was in New York.
是啊，当时我女朋友在纽约。

339
00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:39.630
So I was in LA alone and had no kids or pets or responsibilities.
所以我一个人在洛杉矶，没有孩子、宠物或任何负担。

340
00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:43.010
So that is all just like memorized.
所以那些台词我全都背下来了。

341
00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:52.270
And I think, you know, as an indication of like my obsession sometimes with things, I think it had been lightly suggested.
而且我觉得，这也能看出我有时对事情有多执着，当时只是被轻描淡写地提了一句。

342
00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:57.650
Like here's some scenes that'd be fun for you to, you know, so we could pull clips from it.
就像是说“这里有些片段你可以演一下，这样我们就能剪辑出一些素材”。

343
00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:04.910
And then I memorized the first like 40 minutes of that movie or something, you know, like the cadence of it, the thing.
然后我就把那部电影前40分钟左右的内容全背下来了，你知道，包括那种节奏感，还有各种细节。

344
00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:11.670
And also personally, cause I was like, I don't want anyone who loves diehard to watch this and be like, what is he doing?
而且我个人也是这么想的，因为我不想让任何《虎胆龙威》的影迷看到这一幕时说：“他在干什么？”

345
00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.530
That's not what happens.
“剧情根本不是这样的。”

346
00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.190
You know?
你懂吗？

347
00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.510
You had so much detail.
你处理得太细致了。

348
00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:19.530
Like you would say a line and then you'd go ring, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning.
你演完一句台词，然后还会配音“叮，宁，宁，宁，宁，宁，宁，宁，宁，宁”。

349
00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.550
You're not going to come here.
“你不会来这里的。”

350
00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:23.610
Ring, ning, ning, ning.
“叮，宁，宁，宁。”

351
00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:25.810
I'm like, what is, what is the ring, ning, ning, ning?
我在想，那个什么，什么铃，铃，铃，铃声是什么？

352
00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.150
Is it the big fan?
是那个大风扇吗？

353
00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:28.270
What is that?
那是什么？

354
00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.070
Yeah.
是啊。

355
00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.470
I guess I built out a whole world.
我想我构建出了一个完整的世界。

356
00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:31.790
Yeah.
是啊。

357
00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.530
I thought it would be really fun to go for it or whoever.
我觉得去尝试一下，或者不管是谁去尝试，都会很有趣。

358
00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:39.590
I think also, again, like whoever wrote that episode had approached me and been like, you should go for it.
而且我觉得，还是那句话，写那一集的人当时找过我，说你应该去试试。

359
00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:40.470
Robert Padnick.
罗伯特·帕德尼克。

360
00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:41.470
He loves diehard.
他超爱《虎胆龙威》。

361
00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:41.910
Yeah.
是啊。

362
00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:42.510
He's brilliant.
他是个天才。

363
00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:43.210
Oh yeah.
哦，没错。

364
00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:43.750
He's amazing.
他太棒了。

365
00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.910
When, when I watched all those deleted scenes, I was like, this was hours of memorization.
当我看完那些删减片段时，我在想，这可是花了好几个小时背下来的台词。

366
00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.450
You must've spent so many days on that.
你一定在那上面花了好几天时间。

367
00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:57.150
I would just be in my trailer, you know, in that parking lot, just watching diehard.
我当时就待在拖车里，你知道，就在那个停车场，一直看《虎胆龙威》。

368
00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:59.650
Like, I don't even know if it was on my phone.
我都不知道当时是不是在手机上看的。

369
00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:04.410
I'm trying to, maybe they gave me a DVD of it and I could like play it on the little thing in the trailer or whatever.
我在想，也许他们给了我一张DVD，我可以在拖车里的小设备上播放之类的。

370
00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.310
But like, yeah, yeah.
但总之，是啊，是啊。

371
00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.210
Genuinely hours and hours and hours.
真的是几个小时又几个小时地看。

372
00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:12.270
Well, it's fantastic for anyone out there that has the DVDs.
嗯，对于任何有DVD的人来说，这真是太棒了。

373
00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:18.810
I highly recommend watching all of Jake's performances outside of the episode that live in the deleted scene.
我强烈推荐大家去看看杰克在正片之外，那些存在于删减片段里的表演。

374
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.060
I'm like, it was my one chance.
我在想，那可是我唯一的机会。

375
00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.060
Delete it.
删掉它。

376
00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:29.480
Jake, I have this memory of you joining the cast for that final season.
杰克，我记得你加入剧组是在最后一季。

377
00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:35.360
And there was a group of us who were so delighted to have new people there.
我们当时有一群人，对于有新人加入感到非常高兴。

378
00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:40.580
It was like, you and Clark, I'm afraid we were annoying.
就像你和克拉克，我担心我们当时太烦人了。

379
00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:41.580
I'm afraid.
我担心。

380
00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:46.000
Like, cause we had all talked to each other for eight full years.
因为我们在一起聊了整整八年了。

381
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.440
And now, finally, there were some new people.
现在终于来了些新人。

382
00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:53.440
And it was the most exciting thing.
这简直太让人兴奋了。

383
00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:59.260
I would actually try to, like, not overwhelm you with talking your ear off.
我其实一直在努力克制，不想因为说个不停而让你感到不知所措。

384
00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.300
Because we were just, I mean, the crew included.
因为我们当时，我是说，包括剧组人员在内。

385
00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.840
There was not a new face for so long.
已经很久没有出现过新面孔了。

386
00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.020
I have to know, like, how was it for you?
我必须得问问，你当时感觉如何？

387
00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.680
Well, I've never thought of it in those terMs.
嗯，我从来没从这个角度想过。

388
00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:18.000
Like, it's never crossed my mind to go, all right, you had almost 10 years of working with the same people for months and months.
我从来没想过，好吧，你们和同一群人一起工作了快十年，每个月都在一起。

389
00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:25.680
And, like, the bond that that brings, you also go, man, it'd be nice to not know everyone's life story that I'm here with.
那种羁绊确实很深，但你也会想，天哪，如果不用了解我身边每个人的生活故事该多好。

390
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:26.320
Exactly.
没错。

391
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.160
It'd be nice to have a little mystery.
如果能保留一点神秘感就好了。

392
00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:28.920
Yeah.
是啊。

393
00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:40.940
Um, I, you know, at the time, I just thought, I was just so consumed with, like, you know, don't mess this up.
嗯，你知道，当时我满脑子想的都是，别搞砸了。

394
00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:44.060
Don't be weird around these people.
在这些人面前别表现得太奇怪。

395
00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:46.360
Don't, you know what I mean?
别，你懂我的意思吧？

396
00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:49.460
Like, don't fan out and get weird.
别表现得像个粉丝一样，别太怪异。

397
00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:54.020
And, you know, like, just show up and do your thing and leave.
你知道，就是做好自己的事，然后离开。

398
00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.420
Don't try to make it social.
别试图去搞社交。

399
00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:59.480
Don't, you know, like, nobody's excited that you're here, Jake.
别，你知道，没人因为你的到来而感到兴奋，杰克。

400
00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:00.800
Just do your thing.
做好你自己的事就行了。

401
00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:06.880
So, it's funny years later to hear you go, like, we were thrilled to have new people here.
所以，多年后听到你说“我们很高兴有新人加入”，这真是有趣。

402
00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:12.060
Um, and that you were like, I'm going to play it cool because that's what I was doing.
嗯，你说你当时想“我要装作若无其事”，因为我当时就是这么做的。

403
00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:13.960
I was fully being like, I'm going to play it cool.
我当时完全就是那种心态，我要装作若无其事。

404
00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:14.660
I'm going to play it cool.
我要装作若无其事。

405
00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.080
Like, I'm, hey, it's nice to meet you.
就像是，嘿，很高兴见到你。

406
00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.100
As if I've never seen the show and didn't know it existed.
就好像我从没看过这部剧，也不知道它的存在一样。

407
00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:21.040
Instead of, like, I've seen every episode.
而不是表现得像，我每一集都看过。

408
00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:22.400
It's my favorite program.
这是我最喜欢的节目。

409
00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:22.980
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

410
00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:24.540
Oh, my gosh, yes.
天哪，当然明白。

411
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.780
Okay, so I just watched the episode with my teens.
好的，我刚才和我的孩子们一起看了那一集。

412
00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.480
We did a little bit of a office marathon last night.
我们昨晚进行了一场小型的《办公室》马拉松。

413
00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.060
And we watched the beginning of Moving On.
我们看了《继续前进》的开头。

414
00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.160
And Andy comes back.
安迪回来了。

415
00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:38.900
And he's forgotten that your name is Pete.
他忘了你的名字叫皮特。

416
00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:40.700
He just calls you Plop.
他直接叫你“噗噗”。

417
00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.860
And he's like, Aaron is hooking up with some guy named Pete.
他说，艾琳正和一个叫皮特的家伙约会。

418
00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:48.700
You have a great moment where you're like, I think Andy's called me Plop for so long.
你有一个很棒的瞬间，你说，我觉得安迪叫我“噗噗”太久了。

419
00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.380
He's forgotten my name is Pete.
他已经忘了我的名字是皮特。

420
00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:51.440
Yeah.
是啊。

421
00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.240
That runner was hilarious.
那个梗真是太搞笑了。

422
00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.160
Which is my name, Pete.
也就是我的名字，皮特。

423
00:21:55.940 --> 00:22:00.780
Like, I think then I, now you're, like, I say it again to the camera crew, basically.
就像，我想当时我，现在你，基本上就是对着摄影组又说了一遍。

424
00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:04.620
To be like, that's me, just in case you guys are also not caught up.
为了表示，那就是我，以防你们也没跟上进度。

425
00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:06.100
I'm, I'm Pete.
我，我是皮特。

426
00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:14.160
Yeah, that was, you know, the, is that, Jon Favreau directed one of those.
是啊，那是，你知道，那是乔恩·费儒执导的其中一集。

427
00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:16.880
It might be that, that episode.
可能就是那一集。

428
00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:17.320
Yes.
没错。

429
00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:18.780
And then they made it two.
然后他们把它拍成了两集。

430
00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:20.640
They made it two parts, right.
他们把它做成了上下两部分，对吧。

431
00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:21.180
Yeah.
是的。

432
00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.180
I loved working with him.
我很喜欢和他合作。

433
00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:30.900
It was, like, maybe my favorite big name guest director that we had outside of Harold Ramis.
除了哈罗德·雷米斯之外，他可能是我最喜欢的客座大牌导演了。

434
00:22:31.220 --> 00:22:31.400
Yeah.
是啊。

435
00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:32.580
With Jon Favreau.
和乔恩·费儒一起。

436
00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:37.340
And I know, I'm sorry, that was before he joined us.
我知道，抱歉，那是在他加入我们之前。

437
00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:39.320
Yeah, he's a hero.
是啊，他是位英雄。

438
00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:40.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

439
00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:40.900
Legend.
传奇人物。

440
00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:41.900
Yeah.
是啊。

441
00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:43.660
But Jon Favreau was amazing.
但乔恩·费儒真的很棒。

442
00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:50.420
And they, so, his episode was so good that they didn't want to cut a single minute from it.
而且他们，那一集拍得太好了，他们一分钟都不舍得剪掉。

443
00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:52.720
And so they made it supersized.
所以他们把它做成了超长版。

444
00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:53.760
Yes.
没错。

445
00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:55.040
Yeah.
是啊。

446
00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:58.100
What I remember that he, well, I guess I have a couple things.
我记得他，嗯，我想我有几件事印象深刻。

447
00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:02.300
One is, like, I remember before every scene, he would just go over the moment before.
第一，我记得在每一场戏之前，他都会过一遍之前的剧情。

448
00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:03.520
Yes.
是的。

449
00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:08.720
He would just, as a group, go, like, hey, just to be clear, this person's back.
他会带着大家一起，说，嘿，明确一下，这个人刚回来。

450
00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:10.540
You're feeling this way about it.
你对这件事有这种感觉。

451
00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.880
Maybe you guys feel something else about it.
也许你们对这件事有别的看法。

452
00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:13.240
I don't know.
我不知道。

453
00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.060
That's up to you.
这取决于你们。

454
00:23:14.760 --> 00:23:16.700
And you're worried about this.
而你对此感到担心。

455
00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:20.100
And earlier, we found out about that.
而且早些时候，我们发现了那件事。

456
00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:21.500
So let's just keep that in mind.
所以我们把它记在心里就好。

457
00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:23.320
And, uh, go ahead.
那么，呃，继续吧。

458
00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:28.900
And, you know, like, that clarity, just going back to the basics of, like, where are you coming from?
还有，你知道，那种清晰感，回归到最基础的问题，比如，你从哪里来？

459
00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:29.560
Where are you going?
你要去哪里？

460
00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:30.400
What are you trying to get?
你想要得到什么？

461
00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.480
Yeah, just good scene work.
没错，就是很棒的场景处理。

462
00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:33.840
He was so good with that.
他在这方面做得太好了。

463
00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:34.840
Yeah.
是啊。

464
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:41.900
And letting that add up to something, you know, that if you had all the pieces, then in the edit, he could go, oh, I'll build it from here, you know.
让这些点滴积累成某种东西，你知道，如果你有了所有的素材，那么在剪辑时，他就能说，噢，我可以从这里构建它，你知道的。

465
00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:53.280
And also that he knew story-wise, there was something where I come in, talking to Aaron, I'm asking about mail, Andy's back.
而且他从故事层面也很清楚，有一场戏是我进来，和亚伦说话，我问起邮件的事，安迪回来了。

466
00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:59.280
And there was some kind of back and forth, like, two or four or five lines, something like that.
当时有一些来回的对话，大概两句、四句或五句的样子。

467
00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:02.840
And John was like, just, I know what they're trying to do here.
约翰当时就说，我知道他们在这里想表达什么。

468
00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:06.000
I don't think this really accomplishes it.
我觉得这段对话并没有真正达到目的。

469
00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:13.440
Just come in and look through the mail and look down to Ellie.
你只要走进来，翻翻邮件，然后看向艾莉。

470
00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:21.300
And she'll sort of look up to you, and you can smile, and then just take your mail and go to the desk.
她会抬头看你，你可以微笑一下，然后拿上邮件走到桌边。

471
00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:23.020
And I was like, amazing.
我当时就觉得，太棒了。

472
00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:27.740
Like, that he understood to go, like, maybe we don't need this dialogue.
他能理解到，比如，也许我们不需要这些台词。

473
00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:29.060
Like, just, we get it.
就像是，我们懂了。

474
00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:32.000
We see two people who are into each other.
我们看到了两个互相倾慕的人。

475
00:24:32.140 --> 00:24:34.440
We see this little quiet, private connection.
我们看到了这种安静、私密的连接。

476
00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:41.740
And, like, that means more to the story and to the audience than being quippy with each other.
这对于故事和观众来说，比互相耍嘴皮子更有意义。

477
00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:45.920
Like, that's not actually the thing that those two characters have found in each other.
因为那并不是这两个角色在彼此身上找到的东西。

478
00:24:46.060 --> 00:24:47.620
It's not a sparring partner.
那不是在找吵架的对手。

479
00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:49.260
It's someone that they like to be with.
而是找一个他们喜欢相处的人。

480
00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:50.520
So just be with them.
所以只要和他们待在一起就好。

481
00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:53.840
You know, like, he could see that stuff and go, oh, man.
你知道，他能看出这些东西，然后说，噢，天哪。

482
00:24:54.560 --> 00:24:57.680
And I feel like I'm talking a lot, but I just love the show.
我觉得我话有点多，但我就是太爱这部剧了。

483
00:24:57.820 --> 00:25:02.140
And I don't know, this is, like, a door to memory lane that I didn't know existed.
我不知道，这就像是一扇我从未察觉的通往回忆之路的门。

484
00:25:02.140 --> 00:25:03.160
So it's very exciting.
所以这非常令人兴奋。

485
00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:17.060
But I know Ed, you know, he's like, he finds out that it's me that Aaron has been seeing and now is trying to drive this wedge.
但我知道艾德，你知道，他发现亚伦一直在见的人是我，现在他想从中作梗。

486
00:25:17.520 --> 00:25:26.660
And I think there's outtakes of it where he's going through Wikipedia or, like, you know, WebMD or something.
我想还有一些花絮，他在查维基百科，或者，你知道，WebMD之类的网站。

487
00:25:26.660 --> 00:25:32.000
And it's going, yeah, you know, you never know who has what.
然后他说，是啊，你知道，你永远不知道谁有什么病。

488
00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:42.640
But I just got my test back and I've got and looks over at the screen and then calls Chlamydia Schlamydia because he doesn't know what it is.
但我刚拿到检查结果，我有……然后看向屏幕，接着喊出“衣原体，衣原体”，因为他不知道那是什么。

489
00:25:42.960 --> 00:25:45.220
And but I didn't know he's going to do that.
但我不知道他会那样做。

490
00:25:45.340 --> 00:25:47.180
And I just like lost it.
我当时直接笑喷了。

491
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:51.680
Like, just died laughing at him improv-ing Schlamydia.
就是，看着他即兴发挥“衣原体”那个梗，我笑得不行。

492
00:25:51.680 --> 00:25:55.520
Yeah, that makes it in the episode, too.
没错，那段也放进剧集里了。

493
00:25:56.320 --> 00:25:56.560
Yes.
是的。

494
00:25:56.660 --> 00:25:58.300
Then we had to go back and John was like, do it.
然后我们不得不重拍，约翰说，就这样做。

495
00:25:58.400 --> 00:25:59.120
Yeah, do that.
对，就那样做。

496
00:25:59.300 --> 00:25:59.520
Do that.
就这样做。

497
00:25:59.620 --> 00:25:59.880
Do that.
就这样做。

498
00:26:00.280 --> 00:26:03.500
And had been like, that was another one where he was like, don't worry about the dialogue.
还有一次也是这样，他说，别管台词了。

499
00:26:03.620 --> 00:26:05.580
Like, let's just do one where you come in and.
我们来拍一个你走进来，然后……的版本。

500
00:26:05.580 --> 00:26:10.280
And, you know, that he knows and he knows that, you know, that he knows and let's see what happens.
而且，你知道，他心里有数，他知道，你知道，他心里有数，让我们看看会发生什么。

501
00:26:11.180 --> 00:26:18.160
And so then there's like my proudest performance moment on that whole show is me going like, you know, you were gone.
所以在那整部剧中，我最引以为傲的表演时刻，就是我说出“你知道吗，你已经走了”的那一刻。

502
00:26:18.440 --> 00:26:25.100
Like now admitting it and trying to deal with him and that he's like, I knew it, you know, like that it explodes into this thing.
就像现在承认这一点，并试图去面对他，而他反应过来“我早就知道了”，你知道，那种情绪瞬间爆发了出来。

503
00:26:25.100 --> 00:26:31.320
And that was this semi-organic, like improv from John and Ed and that.
那是一段半即兴的表演，来自约翰、埃德和我。

504
00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:32.640
I was like, oh, this.
当时我就觉得，噢，就是这个。

505
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:33.440
Wow.
哇。

506
00:26:34.020 --> 00:26:42.300
You know, again, as a fan and a love of the show and a participant and all this stuff, like coming together at once, you're like, oh, my God, I can't believe I'm going to do this.
你知道，作为一名粉丝，一个热爱这部剧的人，同时也是参与者，当这一切汇聚在一起时，你会觉得，天哪，我真不敢相信我能做到。

507
00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:45.200
Like, oh, that moment is so good.
真的，那个瞬间太棒了。

508
00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:48.880
I didn't know that story behind that moment is brilliant.
我以前不知道那个瞬间背后的故事，真是太精彩了。

509
00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:50.720
Oh, just all that, man.
噢，就是这一切，伙计。

510
00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:51.100
Yeah.
是啊。

511
00:26:51.440 --> 00:26:51.760
God.
天哪。

512
00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:53.340
So cool, dude.
太酷了，伙计。

513
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:54.240
It's so cool.
真的太酷了。

514
00:26:54.240 --> 00:26:56.980
I just, yeah, man, it makes me so happy to be thinking about it.
我只是，是啊，伙计，想到这些让我感到非常开心。

515
00:27:07.430 --> 00:27:12.150
I just wanted to know if there were, because you were just talking about opening that door to memory lane.
我只是想知道，因为你刚才提到了打开记忆的闸门。

516
00:27:12.490 --> 00:27:22.830
Are there any other like scenes or moments or it could be an on-camera and off-camera moment that come to mind that we haven't talked about?
还有没有其他场景或时刻，无论是镜头前还是镜头后的，是你想到但我们还没聊过的？

517
00:27:24.290 --> 00:27:30.490
Anything that like if you could go back and relive it that you'd be like, oh, I got to do that again.
有没有什么事，如果你能回到过去重温一遍，你会觉得，噢，我一定要再做一次。

518
00:27:31.530 --> 00:27:42.170
I bet there's a hundred that I, you know, I don't know, can't remember or I don't know, but I, but the, but ones I do are like, you know, your final talking head.
我敢说有上百个我可能记不清了，或者不知道，但我记得的，比如你最后的采访镜头。

519
00:27:44.130 --> 00:27:49.170
Like, I think that I have a photo, I think that I was even like, I should not be taking this.
我想我当时甚至拍了张照，我当时心想，我不该拍这个的。

520
00:27:49.650 --> 00:27:53.370
But like, uh, we were all in video village, Jake.
但当时我们都在监视器旁，杰克。

521
00:27:53.730 --> 00:27:56.370
Remember we were all on that couch together watching it.
记得吗，我们都在那张沙发上一起看着它。

522
00:27:56.370 --> 00:27:57.010
Yes.
记得。

523
00:27:57.330 --> 00:27:57.550
Yeah.
是啊。

524
00:27:57.810 --> 00:27:59.670
And I felt like I should not be here.
我当时觉得我不该在那儿。

525
00:27:59.990 --> 00:28:04.210
Like this is, these people have created this thing.
就像是，这些人创造了这部作品。

526
00:28:04.210 --> 00:28:10.790
And I got to like be a bandaid on this, you know, like I'm a snail stuck to the side of the ship.
而我只是像个创可贴一样贴在上面，你知道，就像粘在船边的一只蜗牛。

527
00:28:10.790 --> 00:28:18.450
But these folks built the ship, you know, and going like, I should give them space as if like a loved one was passing.
但这些人造了这艘船，你知道，我当时想，我应该给他们留点空间，就像有人在送别挚爱一样。

528
00:28:18.450 --> 00:28:23.370
And I was, I don't know, someone bringing in Jell-O that was like, whoops, my bad.
而我，不知道，就像是个送果冻进来的人，心想，噢，抱歉，打扰了。

529
00:28:23.650 --> 00:28:28.330
But I just remember being in that room and thinking like, this is nuts.
但我记得当时在那个房间里，心想，这太疯狂了。

530
00:28:28.650 --> 00:28:36.270
Again, like as a participant, as a person on the show and going like, oh man, I've loved my time here.
再次强调，作为一名参与者，作为剧组的一员，我心想，天哪，我爱我在剧组的这段时光。

531
00:28:36.270 --> 00:28:47.510
It's so sad to think this is the end of it, you know, and also as a viewer, as a fan of the show for so many years to go, oh man, I can't believe I'm here.
想到这是终点真是太难过了，你知道，同时作为一名观众，作为这部剧多年的粉丝，心想，天哪，我真不敢相信我在这儿。

532
00:28:47.790 --> 00:28:49.210
I'm inside the thing.
我身处其中。

533
00:28:49.350 --> 00:28:51.730
I'm inside the mothership, like watching it happen.
我身处母舰内部，看着这一切发生。

534
00:28:51.930 --> 00:28:52.970
This is insane.
这太不可思议了。

535
00:28:52.970 --> 00:28:57.770
And I'm here with everybody who's made this thing for almost a decade who, you know what I mean?
而且我和所有制作这部剧近十年的人在一起，你明白我的意思吗？

536
00:28:57.830 --> 00:29:00.730
It was just surreal, surreal then surreal now.
那真是太超现实了，当时超现实，现在回想起来依然超现实。

537
00:29:00.870 --> 00:29:02.650
It's never, I don't know.
永远都是，我不知道。

538
00:29:03.390 --> 00:29:06.250
But other memories riding to the, you know,
还有其他记忆，比如去往……你知道，

539
00:29:07.110 --> 00:29:14.870
being in a van with everybody going to the last table read and the way they had that table read set up with the cameras so that execs could see it back.
和大家一起坐面包车去参加最后一次剧本围读，他们架设摄像机的方式，好让高管们能回看。

540
00:29:14.970 --> 00:29:19.970
Everybody wanted to be a part of it, you know, and the,
每个人都想参与其中，你知道，还有，

541
00:29:20.350 --> 00:29:28.950
after we wrapped and then there was that kind of strange wrap party and then the very cool wrap party and Stephen Merchant being there.
杀青之后，那场奇怪的杀青派对，然后是那场非常酷的杀青派对，斯蒂芬·莫昌特也在场。

542
00:29:28.950 --> 00:29:37.150
And me reintroducing myself to Stephen Merchant, assuming he does not know who I am, you know, even though he's an EP on the show.
我重新向斯蒂芬·莫昌特做了自我介绍，假设他不知道我是谁，你知道，尽管他是这部剧的执行制片人。

543
00:29:37.270 --> 00:29:38.890
And he was like, yeah, no, I know, Jake.
他当时说，不，我知道，杰克。

544
00:29:38.990 --> 00:29:39.950
I've seen every episode.
我每一集都看了。

545
00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:41.170
Like I, I hired you.
是我雇佣的你。

546
00:29:41.290 --> 00:29:41.830
I've seen the edits.
我看过剪辑版。

547
00:29:41.830 --> 00:29:47.290
Like I'm aware, you know, like still to the end being like, oh, pleasure to meet you.
我很清楚，你知道，但我还是坚持到最后说，噢，很高兴见到你。

548
00:29:47.450 --> 00:29:48.870
He was like, yeah, no, we got it.
他当时说，是啊，没关系，我们懂的。

549
00:29:48.970 --> 00:29:49.590
We got it.
我们懂的。

550
00:29:51.510 --> 00:29:58.730
So Jen and I both know moments on the show where we completely lost it and could barely regain our composure.
所以，珍和我都知道剧里有哪些时刻是我们彻底失控，几乎无法恢复镇定的。

551
00:29:59.050 --> 00:30:00.590
Like we lost it.
就像我们笑场了一样。

552
00:30:01.610 --> 00:30:09.530
And I know you said that you broke at the slack line, but was there any other moment where you completely lost it?
我知道你说你在走钢丝那场戏笑场了，但还有没有其他时刻是你完全憋不住笑的？

553
00:30:09.530 --> 00:30:20.780
Like there's a couple of times where, there's a couple of times in the conference room where I really felt like, oh God, I'm going to die here.
比如有几次，在会议室里有几次我真的觉得，天哪，我要死在这里了。

554
00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:21.760
This will be the end.
这简直要了我的命。

555
00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:34.660
And, um, but some of those were like, uh, John, John one time was like, hey, watch this, Brian, make it go on too long.
还有，嗯，有些时候是这样的，比如约翰，有一次约翰说，嘿，布莱恩，看这个，把它演得久一点。

556
00:30:34.660 --> 00:30:36.660
And Brian was like, got it.
布莱恩就说，没问题。

557
00:30:37.020 --> 00:30:53.300
And then at the end, when the scripted scene has finished, you know, Brian as Kevin would just lob in another line or two, like just calling back to his own storyline to be like,
然后在最后，当剧本里的戏份演完时，你知道，布莱恩饰演的凯文会随口再加一两句台词，比如呼应他自己的剧情，就像是说，

558
00:30:53.660 --> 00:31:03.540
but are we going to, you know, and like each time it would just ruin me to be both like, this has been so funny as scripted.
但我们要不要，你知道，每次这都会让我崩溃，因为既觉得剧本写得太搞笑了，

559
00:31:03.540 --> 00:31:09.580
And then someone just freewheeling and going like, ah, I'm going to take over at the end here.
又觉得有人在即兴发挥，说，啊，最后这段我要接管了。

560
00:31:09.700 --> 00:31:12.440
I was like, that is so unbelievably funny to me.
我觉得这对我来说简直好笑得不可思议。

561
00:31:12.860 --> 00:31:16.100
I think there's a lot like, I don't know.
我想有很多这样的时刻，我不知道。

562
00:31:16.220 --> 00:31:19.700
I don't know if there's one where I'm like, I don't know.
我不知道有没有哪一次是我觉得，我不知道。

563
00:31:19.820 --> 00:31:21.520
What are ones, what are the top ones?
有哪些呢，最经典的有哪些？

564
00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:25.580
Do you have any from that season that you go this, I couldn't function.
那一季里有没有哪场戏让你觉得，我完全没法正常工作了？

565
00:31:26.500 --> 00:31:29.700
Well, I have one that's very fresh just because I just watched it.
嗯，我有一个印象很深，因为我刚看过。

566
00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:34.500
But when Aunt Shirley slapped me, she really slapped me.
雪莉阿姨打我耳光的时候，她是真的打了我。

567
00:31:35.080 --> 00:31:42.040
And you can see me sort of like, I have to like bend over because I'm kind of shock laughing.
你可以看到我有点像，我不得不弯下腰，因为我被惊到了，在偷笑。

568
00:31:42.420 --> 00:31:45.080
Like, oh, that really hurt.
就像是，噢，那真的好痛。

569
00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:47.520
She really slapped me.
她是真的打了我。

570
00:31:47.640 --> 00:31:49.280
You're like, got a handful there.
你当时就像是，这下可够受的。

571
00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:49.780
Yeah.
是啊。

572
00:31:49.780 --> 00:31:52.400
But so that was very fresh for me.
所以那次印象非常深刻。

573
00:31:52.680 --> 00:32:03.660
But just the conference room, whenever we all had a moment, whenever we all had a line, and it was just like zipping around the conference room, there was always that great energy.
但只要是在会议室，每当我们大家都有戏份，每当我们每个人都有台词，而且台词在会议室里飞快地来回穿梭时，总有一种很棒的能量。

574
00:32:03.940 --> 00:32:06.520
And we were confined in that tiny space.
而且我们被困在那个狭小的空间里。

575
00:32:06.680 --> 00:32:09.540
And that added to it all day long, being stuck in that space.
整天被困在那个空间里，这更增添了那种氛围。

576
00:32:10.220 --> 00:32:12.440
That's usually when I broke the hardeSt.
那通常是我笑场最严重的时候。

577
00:32:12.440 --> 00:32:16.680
I just remember losing it a lot during the Lice episode.
我只记得在《虱子》那一集里我笑场了很多次。

578
00:32:17.080 --> 00:32:22.400
Kate being so, like, defensive and then bald.
凯特表现得那么防御，然后又秃了头。

579
00:32:23.800 --> 00:32:28.060
And the guilt that my character had over the whole situation.
还有我饰演的角色对整个局面的愧疚感。

580
00:32:28.320 --> 00:32:28.800
Oh, my God.
天哪。

581
00:32:29.060 --> 00:32:32.180
I just remember laughing a lot during that episode.
我只记得那一集我笑得特别多。

582
00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:34.800
As you say that, like, I had forgotten.
你这么一说，我都忘了。

583
00:32:35.640 --> 00:32:37.180
Well, I guess now it reminds me.
嗯，我想现在这提醒了我。

584
00:32:37.180 --> 00:32:41.400
Like, Zach Woods came back for one episode, maybe.
比如，扎克·伍兹回来客串了一集，大概吧。

585
00:32:41.600 --> 00:32:43.480
And I was a fan of his from a distance.
我一直很欣赏他。

586
00:32:43.480 --> 00:32:52.700
And then in the moment, people had been like, they don't really write stuff for him because he's so smart that he kind of has alts for himself, you know,
当时大家都在说，他们其实没怎么给他写台词，因为他太聪明了，他自己就能想出替代方案，你知道，

587
00:32:52.780 --> 00:32:56.100
and that they'd offered for him to be a writer on the show a handful of times.
而且他们曾多次邀请他担任节目的编剧。

588
00:32:56.100 --> 00:32:57.660
And he was like, no, I want to perform.
但他总是说，不，我想表演。

589
00:32:57.820 --> 00:32:58.180
Like, I don't.
就像，我不。

590
00:32:58.440 --> 00:32:59.720
I want to be able to do both.
我想两者兼顾。

591
00:32:59.920 --> 00:33:02.580
And he came in and we're in a conference room.
他来了，我们在会议室里。

592
00:33:02.700 --> 00:33:04.020
It's just there's four of us there.
当时只有我们四个人在那里。

593
00:33:04.020 --> 00:33:11.040
And he, the things he had brought with him in his little, like, dialogue bag of tricks.
他从他那小小的对话锦囊里拿出来的东西，

594
00:33:11.300 --> 00:33:12.900
I was like, holy s**t.
我当时就想，天哪。

595
00:33:13.120 --> 00:33:23.340
Like, it was both what he was presenting and then also if I could try to keep up with him for a moment, like, so fast back into it.
这既在于他呈现的内容，也在于如果我能试着跟上他的节奏，那种飞快的即兴互动。

596
00:33:23.400 --> 00:33:23.680
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

597
00:33:23.680 --> 00:33:28.020
To add to it, not cutting me down, but just to add into the joke of it.
他是在为笑话添砖加瓦，而不是打断我，只是为了让笑话更好笑。

598
00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:31.920
You know, I was like, this is another level.
你知道，我当时想，这简直是另一个境界。

599
00:33:31.920 --> 00:33:37.380
You know, like, this is something I wish I knew what magic trick is happening here.
你知道，这让我很想知道他到底用了什么魔法。

600
00:33:37.500 --> 00:33:39.500
You know, like, yeah, God.
你知道，就是这样，天哪。

601
00:33:39.760 --> 00:33:42.640
I just think, oh, and I, sorry.
我只是觉得，哦，还有我，抱歉。

602
00:33:43.360 --> 00:33:46.700
I know it's, I'm a guest on the show, so you're asking me questions.
我知道，我是节目的嘉宾，所以你是在问我问题。

603
00:33:46.860 --> 00:33:48.140
I still feel like I'm talking a lot about me.
但我还是觉得我一直在说我自己的事。

604
00:33:48.260 --> 00:33:51.500
But I have food poisoning during that episode.
那一集的时候我食物中毒了。

605
00:33:51.500 --> 00:33:58.180
So I would go throw up in my trailer, I didn't know you could call into work, and then come shoot those scenes.
所以我得去休息车里呕吐，我当时不知道还能请假，吐完就回来拍那些戏份。

606
00:33:58.560 --> 00:34:04.060
So I look, like, kind of pallid, you know, in some of those scenes and then, like, go back to my trailer.
所以你看，在那些镜头里我看起来脸色有点苍白，你知道的，拍完就回休息车。

607
00:34:04.120 --> 00:34:04.820
For the lice episode?
是虱子那一集吗？

608
00:34:04.820 --> 00:34:09.640
And just be like, no, for whatever episode Zach came back for.
不，不是，是扎克回来的那一集。

609
00:34:09.640 --> 00:34:15.120
And he hires my ex-girlfriend to then work there.
他雇了我的前女友去那里工作。

610
00:34:15.300 --> 00:34:16.620
Yes, yes, right.
对，对，没错。

611
00:34:16.900 --> 00:34:20.580
And sets us up as this love-hate triangle thing.
然后把我们安排成那种爱恨交织的三角关系。

612
00:34:20.940 --> 00:34:24.260
But that episode I had food poisoning, so I was very sick.
但那一集我食物中毒了，病得很重。

613
00:34:24.260 --> 00:34:34.180
And then also coming in and, like, no food in my system and kind of like, uh, and Zach just, like, throwing heat for an hour and me, like,
而且当时我没吃东西，身体很虚，扎克在那儿火力全开地演了一个小时，而我呢，

614
00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:41.000
giggling at a conference table and then being like, if you'll excuse me to go back into my trailer and be sick.
在会议桌前咯咯笑，然后说，失陪一下，就回休息车去难受了。

615
00:34:41.880 --> 00:34:45.540
But that's one where I couldn't stop laughing, and I thought, like, I'm going to ruin this for him.
但那一集我实在忍不住笑，我想，我肯定会毁了他的表演。

616
00:34:45.740 --> 00:34:47.300
They won't be able to edit around me laughing.
他们肯定没法剪掉我笑场的部分。

617
00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:49.780
I sound wildly unprofessional in that way.
那样听起来我太不专业了。

618
00:34:49.780 --> 00:34:53.480
But just thinking, like, this is too funny.
但我当时就觉得，这太搞笑了。

619
00:34:53.480 --> 00:34:54.860
I won't manage.
我控制不住。

620
00:34:55.880 --> 00:34:58.580
Do you think Pete and Aaron ended up together?
你觉得皮特和亚伦最后在一起了吗？

621
00:34:58.580 --> 00:35:01.900
It's very vague in the finale.
大结局里交代得很模糊。

622
00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:04.580
What were you playing?
你是怎么演的？

623
00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:06.060
What was your decision?
你的决定是什么？

624
00:35:06.800 --> 00:35:09.760
That I think she moves on.
我觉得她向前看了。

625
00:35:10.900 --> 00:35:11.460
Really?
真的吗？

626
00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:13.260
You don't think they end up together?
你不觉得他们最后在一起了？

627
00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:16.860
No, but I think, like, look, I haven't really stayed.
不觉得，而且我觉得，听着，我其实没怎么关注。

628
00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:19.420
Maybe this is different for you.
也许这对你来说不一样。

629
00:35:19.600 --> 00:35:22.340
For me, when people go, like, I'm still close with all my exes.
对我而言，当人们说，我跟所有前任都还保持亲密关系时。

630
00:35:22.420 --> 00:35:24.320
I'm like, you're out of your mind.
我会觉得，你们疯了吧。

631
00:35:24.800 --> 00:35:25.780
But, okay.
不过，好吧。

632
00:35:26.720 --> 00:35:32.020
To me, I'm like, I think Pete and Aaron genuinely, like, stay close.
对我来说，我觉得皮特和亚伦确实是保持着亲密关系。

633
00:35:32.540 --> 00:35:35.960
You know, that they each, like, had this time together.
你知道，他们曾经拥有过那段时光。

634
00:35:35.960 --> 00:35:48.280
And she also finds such deeper, I don't know, clarity and closure in the other storyline for her of, like, her birth mother.
而且她在另一条关于她亲生母亲的故事线里，也找到了更深层的，我不知道，清晰感和解脱感。

635
00:35:48.600 --> 00:35:56.900
And, you know, that I feel like Pete is, like, a part of her life that informs that a little but isn't, like, the guy.
我觉得皮特是她生命中的一部分，这对她有一点影响，但他不是那个“真命天子”。

636
00:35:56.900 --> 00:36:03.280
But in this great way that they actually stay close, that they actually stay, like, really good friends.
但以一种很棒的方式，他们确实保持着亲密，确实一直都是很好的朋友。

637
00:36:03.280 --> 00:36:06.280
And it just isn't the thing.
只是不是那种关系而已。

638
00:36:06.660 --> 00:36:09.140
Like, that's kind of my hope for them.
这就是我对他们的期许吧。

639
00:36:09.900 --> 00:36:10.740
But I don't know.
但我不知道。

640
00:36:10.860 --> 00:36:14.400
Maybe, you know, maybe other people feel differently.
也许，你知道，也许别人有不同的看法。

641
00:36:14.920 --> 00:36:15.620
We'll get mail.
我们会收到观众来信的。

642
00:36:15.820 --> 00:36:16.320
We'll get mail.
我们会收到来信的。

643
00:36:17.940 --> 00:36:18.980
He's wrong.
他错了。

644
00:36:19.500 --> 00:36:19.600
Oh.
哦。

645
00:36:22.640 --> 00:36:27.740
We also always ask people, do you get recognized for being Pete?
我们通常还会问嘉宾，你会因为演了皮特而被认出来吗？

646
00:36:28.180 --> 00:36:31.180
And in your case, what do people call you, Pete or Plop?
对你来说，大家是叫你皮特还是“噗噗”？

647
00:36:31.700 --> 00:36:32.720
Yeah, it's Plop.
是“噗噗”。

648
00:36:33.020 --> 00:36:33.960
Plop, for sure.
肯定是“噗噗”。

649
00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:35.180
Plop, definitely.
绝对是“噗噗”。

650
00:36:36.620 --> 00:36:37.080
Yeah.
没错。

651
00:36:37.420 --> 00:36:38.280
Aw, to an extent.
噢，某种程度上是吧。

652
00:36:40.180 --> 00:36:43.620
It is, you know, you go, that's better than not being recognized.
你知道的，你去的时候，心想总比没人认出来要好。

653
00:36:43.780 --> 00:36:44.240
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

654
00:36:44.280 --> 00:36:45.020
That's very nice.
那真的很不错。

655
00:36:45.260 --> 00:36:46.360
But also, like.
但同时，怎么说呢。

656
00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:47.420
Oh, great.
噢，太棒了。

657
00:36:47.420 --> 00:36:51.800
Like, it's the difference that someone goes, like, were you Plop on the office?
就像是有人问你，嘿，你是不是《办公室》里的“噗噗”？这和那种感觉是不一样的。

658
00:36:51.920 --> 00:36:53.040
And you go, yeah, man, that's me.
然后你回答，对啊，伙计，就是我。

659
00:36:53.140 --> 00:36:53.320
Totally.
完全没错。

660
00:36:53.940 --> 00:36:57.300
Or when, like, at Home Depot, someone's like, Plop.
或者像是在家得宝，有人喊你，噗噗。

661
00:36:57.620 --> 00:36:58.920
You go, like, hey, man.
你就会说，嘿，伙计。

662
00:36:59.600 --> 00:37:00.200
Hey, bud.
嘿，哥们。

663
00:37:00.660 --> 00:37:01.680
Can we not yell that?
咱们能别那么大声喊吗？

664
00:37:02.320 --> 00:37:03.160
You know, like, that's.
你知道，那真的。

665
00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:04.860
That's a problem.
那是个问题。

666
00:37:05.360 --> 00:37:06.240
You know, like.
你知道，就像是。

667
00:37:06.780 --> 00:37:09.340
It just is that variation of the interaction.
这只是互动方式的不同。

668
00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:11.800
Because ultimately, like, it's not the name.
因为归根结底，这无关名字。

669
00:37:11.920 --> 00:37:14.140
It's just, like, one feels like a human interaction.
只是，其中一种感觉像是人与人的交流。

670
00:37:14.380 --> 00:37:14.640
Right.
没错。

671
00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:17.500
And one feels like, I don't know.
而另一种感觉，我不知道。

672
00:37:18.160 --> 00:37:18.580
Weird.
很奇怪。

673
00:37:18.980 --> 00:37:19.540
It is.
确实。

674
00:37:19.760 --> 00:37:21.000
But yes, it's sometimes Pete.
但没错，有时候是皮特。

675
00:37:21.200 --> 00:37:21.760
Sometimes Pete.
有时候是皮特。

676
00:37:22.360 --> 00:37:24.480
Everyone's like, well, I get, green is whore-ish.
每个人都说，好吧，我知道，绿色看起来很风骚。

677
00:37:24.680 --> 00:37:29.720
And I'm like, can we dial that one down, folks?
我就说，各位，咱们能收敛点吗？

678
00:37:29.740 --> 00:37:31.220
We can put that one to bed, gang.
伙计们，咱们能别提这茬了吗。

679
00:37:31.380 --> 00:37:31.980
That's all right.
没关系的。

680
00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:33.560
My kids are here.
我的孩子们在这儿呢。

681
00:37:33.800 --> 00:37:34.200
That's right.
没错。

682
00:37:34.200 --> 00:37:36.160
I don't need to explain what whore-ish means.
我可不想解释“风骚”是什么意思。

683
00:37:36.300 --> 00:37:36.980
Thank you.
谢谢。

684
00:37:37.100 --> 00:37:38.540
To an entire middle school.
对着一整个初中生解释。

685
00:37:38.960 --> 00:37:39.620
Like, what the.
搞什么鬼。

686
00:37:39.760 --> 00:37:40.360
Come on, guy.
拜托，老兄。

687
00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:43.980
Did you take anything from set when it wrapped?
剧集杀青的时候，你从片场拿走什么东西了吗？

688
00:37:44.140 --> 00:37:45.540
Because we all took a little something.
因为我们每个人都拿了一点小纪念品。

689
00:37:46.380 --> 00:37:47.620
I was too afraid.
我当时太害怕了。

690
00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:48.760
Aw.
噢。

691
00:37:48.960 --> 00:37:49.480
Too afraid.
太害怕了。

692
00:37:49.740 --> 00:37:50.420
Too afraid.
太害怕了。

693
00:37:51.140 --> 00:37:55.380
I know now that's like, I should have just, like, brought a duffel bag and been like,
我现在知道了，我当时真应该带个行李袋，然后说，

694
00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:56.960
it's all mine.
这些全是我的。

695
00:37:56.960 --> 00:37:57.420
I'm taking it.
我要带走它们。

696
00:37:57.480 --> 00:37:58.200
No one will know.
没人会发现的。

697
00:38:00.080 --> 00:38:05.960
No, I was sure that I'd get a call and people would be like, did you take the stapler?
不，我当时确信我会接到电话，有人会问，你是不是拿了订书机？

698
00:38:08.760 --> 00:38:11.320
No, I think I maybe have, like, a script.
不，我想我可能留着一份剧本。

699
00:38:11.620 --> 00:38:13.120
Maybe, like, a final script.
可能是一份最终剧本。

700
00:38:13.380 --> 00:38:14.340
Something like that.
诸如此类的东西。

701
00:38:14.620 --> 00:38:15.060
All right.
好的。

702
00:38:15.060 --> 00:38:19.900
I wanted to share with you that we noticed we have all the call sheets because everyone's
我想和大家分享一下，我们发现我们拥有所有的通告单，因为自从珍娜和我开始做这个播客以来，

703
00:38:19.900 --> 00:38:22.280
been so amazing since Jenna and I started this podcaSt.
每个人都太棒了。

704
00:38:22.320 --> 00:38:27.300
They have just shared with us shooting drafts and candy bag alts and call sheets.
他们和我们分享了拍摄剧本、糖果袋备选方案和通告单。

705
00:38:27.300 --> 00:38:27.420
Oh, man.
天哪。

706
00:38:27.660 --> 00:38:30.060
So we've really been able to dig in, you know?
所以我们真的能够深入研究，你知道吗？

707
00:38:31.020 --> 00:38:35.920
And one of the things I noticed on the back of the call sheets for season eight, they've
我注意到第八季通告单背面的一件事，

708
00:38:35.920 --> 00:38:38.120
actually stopped for season nine.
到了第九季他们实际上停止了这样做。

709
00:38:38.300 --> 00:38:39.100
I'm not sure why.
我不确定为什么。

710
00:38:39.280 --> 00:38:43.720
But on the back of the call sheets for season eight, there was a little section where it
但在第八季通告单的背面，有一个小版块，

711
00:38:43.720 --> 00:38:45.520
was like, get to know your cast and crew.
内容是了解你的演职人员。

712
00:38:45.860 --> 00:38:48.960
And they picked a person and asked them five questions.
他们会挑选一个人，问他们五个问题。

713
00:38:49.300 --> 00:38:51.280
And it was on the back of every call sheet.
每一张通告单背面都有。

714
00:38:51.420 --> 00:38:55.700
And I am loving them because the questions are fantastic.
我非常喜欢这些，因为问题太棒了。

715
00:38:57.300 --> 00:38:59.800
And we asked these to Bryan Cranston.
我们问过布莱恩·科兰斯顿这些问题。

716
00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:03.800
And I was like, oh, my gosh, Jenna, we have to ask these to every guest moving forward because
当时我就想，天哪，珍娜，我们以后必须问每一位嘉宾这些问题，因为

717
00:39:03.800 --> 00:39:05.900
these questions are so fun.
这些问题太有趣了。

718
00:39:06.180 --> 00:39:07.540
So here they are.
所以，问题来了。

719
00:39:07.740 --> 00:39:12.160
The first question is, what was your first entertainment job?
第一个问题是，你的第一份娱乐业工作是什么？

720
00:39:12.780 --> 00:39:19.040
Oh, well, the first, like, real professional, I was 16.
哦，嗯，第一份，算是真正的专业工作，我当时16岁。

721
00:39:19.580 --> 00:39:20.940
Yeah, 16 or 17.
对，16或17岁。

722
00:39:21.220 --> 00:39:26.060
And I grew up in Vermont, the Bread Loaf Campus of Middlebury College in the summer.
我在佛蒙特州长大，夏天在明德学院的布雷德洛夫校区。

723
00:39:26.060 --> 00:39:31.360
I would do a language program and they would also have people from theater in Providence
我会参加一个语言项目，他们也会邀请普罗维登斯的戏剧界人士

724
00:39:31.360 --> 00:39:32.500
come up and do shows.
过来表演。

725
00:39:32.680 --> 00:39:40.540
So I was in Tom Stoppard's Acadia when I was like 16, I think 17.
所以我大概16或17岁的时候，参演了汤姆·斯托帕德的《阿卡迪亚》。

726
00:39:41.780 --> 00:39:45.120
And, you know, it's just for the summer, but was like working with professional actors
你知道，那只是为了过夏天，但能和专业演员一起工作，

727
00:39:45.120 --> 00:39:47.600
and knew I wanted to be an actor at that point.
从那时起我就知道我想成为一名演员。

728
00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:50.240
So that was like my first ever.
所以那是我有史以来的第一份工作。

729
00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:55.420
Oh, Jake, that makes my theater nerd heart swell so much.
哦，杰克，这让我的戏剧书呆子之心感到无比澎湃。

730
00:39:56.120 --> 00:39:56.780
All right.
好的。

731
00:39:56.940 --> 00:39:58.320
I have the next question.
我有下一个问题。

732
00:39:58.940 --> 00:40:00.960
Do you speak any other languages?
你会说其他语言吗？

733
00:40:02.320 --> 00:40:02.800
No.
不会。

734
00:40:03.160 --> 00:40:04.200
Language of the heart.
心之语言。

735
00:40:04.520 --> 00:40:05.180
No, I don't.
不，我不会。

736
00:40:05.320 --> 00:40:05.880
I don't.
我不会。

737
00:40:06.220 --> 00:40:10.080
I'm working on Italian, but it's not going quickly.
我正在学意大利语，但进展不快。

738
00:40:10.960 --> 00:40:12.140
So no, the answer's no.
所以不，答案是不会。

739
00:40:12.340 --> 00:40:14.380
What was the goal in wanting to learn Italian?
你想学意大利语的目标是什么？

740
00:40:14.680 --> 00:40:19.780
Was it, I'm going to go there and I'm going to be, like, is what, why Italian?
是因为你想去那里，想成为……为什么是意大利语？

741
00:40:20.920 --> 00:40:26.940
I spent a very small amount of time there maybe 10 years ago and traveled around in Italy and
大约10年前我在那里待过很短一段时间，在意大利各地旅行，

742
00:40:26.940 --> 00:40:29.320
thought, like, this is it.
当时就想，就是这里了。

743
00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:32.600
This is where I would move tomorrow.
这就是我明天就会搬去的地方。

744
00:40:32.980 --> 00:40:34.040
Like, any part of it.
任何地方都行。

745
00:40:34.620 --> 00:40:36.860
Tuscany, Umbria, down to the coaSt.
托斯卡纳、翁布里亚，一直到海岸。

746
00:40:36.860 --> 00:40:40.240
I mean, like, I just was totally taken with it.
我是说，我完全被它迷住了。

747
00:40:42.500 --> 00:40:48.060
And, you know, always honestly have one foot in going, like, maybe I'll move to Italy.
而且，你知道，老实说，我一直有一只脚在门外，想着，也许我会搬到意大利去。

748
00:40:48.520 --> 00:40:50.000
You know, like, I have kids now.
你知道，我现在有孩子了。

749
00:40:50.120 --> 00:40:50.760
I'm married, whatever.
我结婚了，诸如此类的。

750
00:40:50.880 --> 00:40:52.420
But go, like, let's go.
但还是会想，走吧，我们走吧。

751
00:40:53.200 --> 00:40:54.920
Like, this business is so remote.
这个行业真的很远程。

752
00:40:56.260 --> 00:40:58.460
I rarely shoot in New York or LA anyways.
反正我很少在纽约或洛杉矶拍戏。

753
00:40:58.860 --> 00:41:03.860
There's no reason for me to go, like, I need to be a train ride away from the city.
我没理由非要去那儿，我只需要离城市坐火车就能到的距离就行。

754
00:41:03.860 --> 00:41:06.780
It's like, yeah, if I want to do a play, that's true.
如果我想演舞台剧的话，那确实有必要。

755
00:41:07.120 --> 00:41:14.220
But the reality of mostly what my work is, is, like, sending in self-tapes, meeting people over Zoom.
但我的工作现状大多是录试镜带、通过Zoom和人开会。

756
00:41:15.040 --> 00:41:19.300
You know, maybe an offer, but really that's kind of rare.
你知道，偶尔会有邀约，但那其实挺少见的。

757
00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:21.140
So, like, I could live anywhere.
所以，我住哪儿都行。

758
00:41:21.500 --> 00:41:24.640
And why not pick up and go to Florence?
为什么不干脆搬去佛罗伦萨呢？

759
00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:26.800
Why not go to Siena, you know?
为什么不去锡耶纳呢，你说呢？

760
00:41:27.260 --> 00:41:37.800
So, and if we were to do that, I'd like to be engaged in a culture and not just, like, an expat floating around the prototypical American to go, like, anyone here speak English?
所以，如果我们真要这么做，我希望能融入当地文化，而不是像个典型的美国外籍人士那样，到处晃悠着问：有人会说英语吗？

761
00:41:38.100 --> 00:41:38.520
Right, right.
没错，没错。

762
00:41:38.520 --> 00:41:39.260
English, anybody.
英语，有人会吗？

763
00:41:39.680 --> 00:41:40.280
But we'll see.
但我们走着瞧吧。

764
00:41:40.600 --> 00:41:46.280
Well, that folds into question number three on the call sheet is, what's a place you've been to that you've loved?
好吧，这正好引出了通告单上的第三个问题：你去过哪些让你流连忘返的地方？

765
00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:50.100
So, I think that's for you, Italy?
我想这题是问你的，意大利？

766
00:41:50.540 --> 00:41:51.760
Italy, to be sure.
肯定是意大利。

767
00:41:51.760 --> 00:41:52.820
And also, I mean, London.
还有，我是说，伦敦。

768
00:41:53.060 --> 00:41:53.300
I don't know.
我不知道。

769
00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:54.220
I've spent a little time in London.
我在伦敦待过一段时间。

770
00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:59.320
I thought this is, I would also, you know, it's the most expensive city maybe in the world.
我觉得这地方……我也想去，你知道，那可能是世界上物价最高的城市。

771
00:42:00.560 --> 00:42:03.060
But London I just thought was wonderful.
但我觉得伦敦真是太棒了。

772
00:42:03.760 --> 00:42:04.100
Yeah.
是啊。

773
00:42:04.620 --> 00:42:05.280
I don't know.
我不知道。

774
00:42:05.400 --> 00:42:07.300
I think that all sounds pretty fantastic.
我觉得这些听起来都很棒。

775
00:42:07.700 --> 00:42:08.540
I want to go.
我想去。

776
00:42:09.400 --> 00:42:10.640
You know, I had friends.
你知道，我以前有朋友。

777
00:42:10.640 --> 00:42:11.980
I had friends in my 20s.
我二十多岁时有几个朋友。

778
00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:16.380
Of course, they didn't have kids yet, you know, but they decided to go live in Italy for a year.
当然，他们那时还没孩子，但他们决定去意大利住一年。

779
00:42:16.800 --> 00:42:19.680
And they went and they lived in Italy for a year and they loved it.
他们真的去了，在意大利住了一年，而且非常喜欢那里。

780
00:42:19.860 --> 00:42:23.240
And I think they think back to that time in their life so fondly.
我觉得他们现在回想起那段时光，依然觉得非常美好。

781
00:42:23.400 --> 00:42:24.560
And I grew up overseas.
而且我是在海外长大的。

782
00:42:25.160 --> 00:42:27.200
So, Jake, I'm saying go for it.
所以，杰克，我的建议是去吧。

783
00:42:27.560 --> 00:42:27.610
Yeah.
是啊。

784
00:42:27.700 --> 00:42:28.460
Where did you grow up?
你在哪儿长大的？

785
00:42:28.640 --> 00:42:29.500
Where were you overseas?
你在海外的什么地方？

786
00:42:29.780 --> 00:42:32.100
I lived 12 years in Jakarta, Indonesia.
我在印度尼西亚的雅加达住了12年。

787
00:42:32.900 --> 00:42:33.840
Oh, my God.
天哪。

788
00:42:34.040 --> 00:42:36.260
What was there that your family was there for?
你家人是因为什么去那儿的？

789
00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:36.640
What was that?
那是怎么回事？

790
00:42:36.700 --> 00:42:40.740
My dad was a drilling engineer and he was transferred there in the 70s.
我父亲是名钻井工程师，70年代被调到了那里。

791
00:42:40.860 --> 00:42:41.840
And I grew up there.
我就在那儿长大的。

792
00:42:42.780 --> 00:42:44.760
I loved that chapter of my life.
我非常怀念人生的那段时光。

793
00:42:44.880 --> 00:42:48.820
So, and I think you just, it's such an education.
所以，我觉得那真的是一种教育。

794
00:42:48.880 --> 00:42:50.600
So, I don't want to get in trouble here.
我可不想惹麻烦。

795
00:42:50.700 --> 00:42:52.540
I don't want to step in your business with your wife.
我不想干涉你和你妻子的事。

796
00:42:52.740 --> 00:42:53.600
But I'm just saying.
但我只是说说而已。

797
00:42:53.700 --> 00:42:54.520
She's into it.
她其实很感兴趣。

798
00:42:54.680 --> 00:42:55.560
She's like, let's go.
她甚至说，我们走吧。

799
00:42:55.700 --> 00:42:56.120
I'm saying go for it.
我是说，去吧。

800
00:42:56.380 --> 00:42:57.020
For real.
认真的。

801
00:42:57.200 --> 00:42:57.340
Yeah.
是啊。

802
00:42:57.440 --> 00:42:59.140
No, you're tipping the scale.
不，你这是在偏袒。

803
00:42:59.500 --> 00:43:03.480
Well, if office ladies come to Italy, we will find you.
好吧，如果办公室的女士们来意大利，我们会去找你的。

804
00:43:03.720 --> 00:43:04.960
You've always got a place to sit.
你总会有地方坐的。

805
00:43:05.100 --> 00:43:06.480
You'll always be welcome in our house.
我们家永远欢迎你。

806
00:43:07.400 --> 00:43:08.440
Pasta and pools.
有意大利面，有泳池。

807
00:43:09.400 --> 00:43:13.160
Next question is, what do you like to do on the weekends?
下一个问题是，你周末喜欢做什么？

808
00:43:16.100 --> 00:43:19.400
I mean, I've got two little boys.
我是说，我有两个小男孩。

809
00:43:19.600 --> 00:43:22.600
So, it's, the weekends are not my own.
所以，周末的时间都不属于我。

810
00:43:22.800 --> 00:43:23.280
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

811
00:43:23.340 --> 00:43:24.440
It's like when they're in school.
就像他们上学的时候那样。

812
00:43:25.700 --> 00:43:28.680
On the weekends, what do I really like to do?
周末的话，我真正喜欢做什么呢？

813
00:43:29.140 --> 00:43:32.240
If I get the chance, I love running.
如果有机会，我喜欢跑步。

814
00:43:32.500 --> 00:43:33.580
I love trail running.
我喜欢越野跑。

815
00:43:33.580 --> 00:43:36.500
If I can get away for just a little bit to do that.
如果我能抽空溜出去跑一会儿的话。

816
00:43:36.780 --> 00:43:39.520
Or, boy, reading.
或者，天哪，看书。

817
00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:41.980
If I can get like a half hour in of just reading.
如果我能有半小时时间只用来读书。

818
00:43:42.460 --> 00:43:43.920
Boy, that's a pleasure.
天哪，那真是一种享受。

819
00:43:44.180 --> 00:43:46.700
You're so obviously the parent of small children.
你一看就是那种有小孩的家长。

820
00:43:47.820 --> 00:43:49.860
Because I remember these days.
因为我记得那些日子。

821
00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:50.720
A shower.
洗个澡。

822
00:43:51.020 --> 00:43:51.360
Yes.
没错。

823
00:43:51.680 --> 00:43:53.780
An uninterrupted shower.
一个不被打扰的澡。

824
00:43:54.080 --> 00:43:54.220
Yeah.
是啊。

825
00:43:54.720 --> 00:43:54.960
Okay.
好吧。

826
00:43:55.120 --> 00:43:56.720
Last question, Jake.
最后一个问题，杰克。

827
00:43:57.420 --> 00:44:00.280
What is your favorite midnight snack?
你最喜欢的宵夜是什么？

828
00:44:02.760 --> 00:44:03.580
Cold pizza.
冷披萨。

829
00:44:04.840 --> 00:44:05.240
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

830
00:44:05.880 --> 00:44:06.220
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

831
00:44:06.760 --> 00:44:07.160
I'll eat.
我会吃。

832
00:44:07.160 --> 00:44:07.920
I'll order pizza.
我会点披萨。

833
00:44:08.600 --> 00:44:10.280
Eat too much of it the first time.
第一次吃的时候吃太多。

834
00:44:11.400 --> 00:44:13.000
Convince myself I won't have any later.
说服自己待会儿不会再吃了。

835
00:44:13.480 --> 00:44:14.480
Put the kids to bed.
把孩子们哄睡。

836
00:44:14.680 --> 00:44:15.580
Put something on.
放点什么节目看。

837
00:44:15.680 --> 00:44:16.620
Be like, do you want a snack?
然后问，你想吃点宵夜吗？

838
00:44:17.320 --> 00:44:18.700
My wife's like, I'm good, dude.
我老婆会说，不用了，伙计。

839
00:44:18.720 --> 00:44:19.920
I had too much for dinner.
我晚饭吃太撑了。

840
00:44:20.080 --> 00:44:20.880
I'm like, yeah, no, totally.
我会说，是啊，没错，完全同意。

841
00:44:21.320 --> 00:44:23.620
And then go downstairs and like, make the coffee.
然后下楼去，比如，煮杯咖啡。

842
00:44:23.720 --> 00:44:24.400
Let the dog out.
放狗出去。

843
00:44:24.560 --> 00:44:25.580
Eat two pieces of pizza.
吃两块披萨。

844
00:44:25.860 --> 00:44:26.960
Be like, what are you doing?
心里想，你在干什么呢？

845
00:44:27.260 --> 00:44:28.180
What is happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

846
00:44:29.100 --> 00:44:29.920
So it's that.
所以就是那个。

847
00:44:30.100 --> 00:44:35.520
And also, man, of late, frosted mini wheats has been like, they're just in there.
还有，伙计，最近的话，糖霜迷你麦片一直都在那儿，它们就在那儿放着。

848
00:44:35.540 --> 00:44:37.460
And I think, oh, that'll fill me up a little.
然后我想，噢，那能让我填填肚子。

849
00:44:37.580 --> 00:44:38.300
It's a little sweet.
有点甜。

850
00:44:38.460 --> 00:44:39.540
It's a little whatever, you know.
反正就是那样，你懂的。

851
00:44:39.720 --> 00:44:42.460
And like, we have these poor tubs.
我们还有这些简陋的塑料桶。

852
00:44:42.580 --> 00:44:45.060
It's not just the box, you know, keeping it all real organized.
不仅仅是盒子，你知道的，要保持一切井井有条。

853
00:44:46.460 --> 00:44:53.160
And, but I won't like put it in a bowl because I'm convinced, you know, I'm convinced I'm going to have like two little handfuls.
而且，我不会把它倒进碗里，因为我坚信，你知道，我坚信我只会抓两小把吃。

854
00:44:53.160 --> 00:44:53.780
And that'll be that.
那样就够了。

855
00:44:53.940 --> 00:44:58.120
But instead, I probably put away like half a bag of cereal and then go like, what?
但实际上，我可能会吃掉半袋麦片，然后心想，怎么回事？

856
00:44:58.320 --> 00:44:59.440
Dude, it's midnight.
老兄，都半夜了。

857
00:44:59.960 --> 00:45:02.900
Like, come on, bud.
拜托，伙计。

858
00:45:03.120 --> 00:45:04.440
Also, why run?
再说，为什么要跑步？

859
00:45:04.560 --> 00:45:04.980
You know what I mean?
你懂我的意思吗？

860
00:45:05.120 --> 00:45:06.740
Just why run and go to the gym?
为什么要跑步去健身房呢？

861
00:45:06.920 --> 00:45:11.920
Then from 11 to 12, you're going to do your own at home fourth meal.
然后从11点到12点，你还要在家里给自己加餐，吃第四顿饭。

862
00:45:12.400 --> 00:45:14.980
You know, remember when Taco Bell made that a thing?
记得塔可钟（Taco Bell）曾经把这当成一个卖点吗？

863
00:45:15.220 --> 00:45:16.960
They were just legit like, go ahead.
他们当时简直就是直接说，尽管吃吧。

864
00:45:17.080 --> 00:45:19.940
Have 25% more food than anyone's ever recommended.
摄入比任何建议量多出25%的食物。

865
00:45:20.220 --> 00:45:20.640
Fourth meal.
第四顿饭。

866
00:45:20.940 --> 00:45:21.380
Oh.
哦。

867
00:45:22.720 --> 00:45:23.360
All right.
好吧。

868
00:45:23.560 --> 00:45:23.900
Cool.
酷。

869
00:45:25.060 --> 00:45:25.380
Yeah.
是啊。

870
00:45:25.600 --> 00:45:26.360
We'll do that.
我们就这么干。

871
00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:27.840
We're into it.
我们很乐意。

872
00:45:28.600 --> 00:45:29.300
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

873
00:45:29.420 --> 00:45:33.800
So that's pizza, pizza, roasted mini-wheats, and yeah.
所以就是披萨、披萨、烤麦片，还有别的。

874
00:45:37.070 --> 00:45:37.530
Nutritious.
营养丰富。

875
00:45:38.150 --> 00:45:41.630
Super, you're packing in some extra nutrition.
太棒了，你还额外补充了一些营养。

876
00:45:42.630 --> 00:45:45.130
I love not committing to a bowl, though.
不过，我喜欢这种不倒进碗里的吃法。

877
00:45:45.310 --> 00:45:45.910
That is me.
我就是这样。

878
00:45:45.990 --> 00:45:49.090
I'm like, if I only take a few handfuls of M&Ms, is it really anything?
我会想，如果我只抓几把M&M豆吃，那真的算吃了什么吗？

879
00:45:49.410 --> 00:45:50.890
Because I didn't put it in a container.
因为我没把它倒进容器里。

880
00:45:51.290 --> 00:45:52.150
It's just a few.
就只是几颗而已。

881
00:45:52.150 --> 00:45:52.750
Right.
没错。

882
00:45:53.070 --> 00:45:53.810
And I doubled it.
然后我吃了一倍的量。

883
00:45:54.150 --> 00:45:54.590
Yeah.
是啊。

884
00:45:55.070 --> 00:45:55.490
Yeah.
是啊。

885
00:45:55.610 --> 00:45:58.930
And then by October 10th, you're like, somehow we're out of candy for Halloween.
然后到了10月10号，你就会发现，万圣节的糖果不知怎么就没了。

886
00:45:59.190 --> 00:46:01.110
I don't know how that happened, but.
我不知道是怎么发生的，但是。

887
00:46:02.710 --> 00:46:03.410
Wasn't me.
不是我干的。

888
00:46:03.550 --> 00:46:04.510
